        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. REPLAY: Pentagon press conference on war in Middle East Issued on: 19/03/2026 - 15:06 US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said Thursday there is no \"time frame\" for ending the US-Israeli war against Iran, which was launched three weeks ago. \"We wouldn't want to set a definitive time frame,\" Hegseth told a news conference, adding that \"we're very much on track\" and that President Donald Trump will be the one to decide when to stop. Hegseth also addressed a report that the Pentagon has requested more than $200 billion in additional funding from Congress to pay for the conflict. Energy prices soar, Iran and US trade threats after Qatar gas hit 19/03/2026 'Free France': Macron reveals name of Europe's largest warship 19/03/2026 Iran: Saudi Arabia warns of 'military action' over repeated attacks 19/03/2026 Middle East Iran women's football team return after asylum tussle 19/03/2026 Gaza's Eid celebrations highlighted by losses amid ongoing conflict 19/03/2026 EU leaders pile pressure on Hungary's Orban to lift block on Ukraine loan 19/03/2026 Trump threatens to strike world's largest gas field if Iran attacks Qatar again 19/03/2026 Who is running Iran? Top leadership decimated by US-Israeli strikes 19/03/2026 Iraq caught in crossfire of Middle East war 19/03/2026"
